2026-01-08 02:04:08 | INFO | Q675 id=BV1BPRnYAEx6_00-14-34_00-14-40 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To solve the problem, let's analyze the information provided in the audio:\n\n1. The price of one steak is over $50, approximately 400 RMB.\n2. If each person gets one steak, the total cost is 1600 RMB.\n\nNow, let's calculate the number of people:\n\n- The total cost for the steaks is 1600 RMB.\n- Each steak costs 400 RMB.\n\nTo find the number of people, we divide the total cost by the cost per steak:\n\n\[ \text{Number of people} = \frac{\text{Total cost}}{\text{Cost per steak}} = \frac{1600 \text{ RMB}}{400 \text{ RMB/steak}} = 4 \]\n\nBased on this calculation, the total number of people is 4.\n\nAnswer: \(\boxed{C}\)
